{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/mage-the-ascension/1149378-renaissance-mage-and-wod-1300-s-to-1600-s","id":1149378,"title":"Renaissance Mage and WOD 1300's to 1600's","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Mage: The Ascension"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-10-13T06:06:05-07:00","id":1149378,"title":"Renaissance Mage and WOD 1300's to 1600's","content":"Well is the new old WOD Renaissance source book for Mage and the rest of the world going to cover 1300's to 1600's?, the old one only went up to 1500. I need it to cover the entire Renasissance period of time,<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T09:46:21-07:00","id":1149453,"title":"","content":"I am not aware of a new book regarding the renaissance being in the making, unless I missed something about new <i>Sorceror's Crusade</i> books coming out.<br /> <br /> What is in the pipeline some years away is <i>Victorian Mage</i>, and that certainly won't cover that timespan - the reign of Queen Victoria was around 1837 to 1901. A very, very important timespan in the world of Mage, but not a long one in total.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://is.gd/wodchart\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Probability Chart</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodcalc\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Dice Statistics Calculator</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodarmor\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Armor System</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage\" target=\"_blank\">cWoD Alternative Damage Roll System</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/woddamage2\" target=\"_blank\">My explanation of cWoD Damage Levels</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodstrength\" target=\"_blank\">'Interesting' Strength Attribute Stuff</a><br /> <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodboom\" target=\"_blank\">EXPLOSIVE cWoD STUFF!</a> ||| <a href=\"https://is.gd/wodheresy\" target=\"_blank\">How Technocrats don't think they are Mages</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6606-ambrosia","name":"Ambrosia","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6606_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1567"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-13T13:31:58-07:00","id":1149514,"title":"","content":"Is there something in particular that happened between 1500 and 1600 that you'd like an official book answer about?<br /> <br /> Even if Sorcerer's Crusade (even some sort of SC20 book) never does, some of the books have at least touched on specific events in timelines and the like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T15:10:27-07:00","id":1151122,"title":"","content":"Well I just want Sorcerer's Crusade to cover 1300's to 1600's not stop at 1500's, I like Sorcerer's Crusade setting for Mage it's just I want the Full Renaissance timeframe covered.<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-10-19T19:35:59-07:00","id":1151187,"title":"","content":"Well, as we have no confirmation of a new SC book for 20th, not much we can do there. Though Revised/20th Dark Ages did touch more on the later parts of the era and how the end of that period was a big turning point for vampires. So it's possible a new SC might opt to do the same and pay more attention to the later parts of the era instead of the earlier.<br /> <br /> Seems like, for now, all you're get are the various time-lines and such that talk about what happened during the periods not covered by SC or modern Mage.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-23T01:59:31-08:00","id":1169854,"title":"","content":"I just want a more proper cover of the Timeframe, that's all.<br /> <br /> LW","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3380-martian1912","name":"Martian1912","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"40"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T11:41:52-08:00","id":1170247,"title":"","content":"Sounds like you are going to need to crack some history books and spend on quality time on the White Wolf wiki to hunt down the various timelines (because you'll probably want more specific info than you will find on the overall timeline) if that's what you want. To a great degree there's not a lot of change to the actual fundamentals of mages at the time that I'm aware of. Not like, say, the Victorian Era. No new Sects. Maybe a few going down the tubes, like the whole Cabal/High Guild/Ksirafai takedown of the Craftmasons. Probably some Houses come and go in the Hermetics.<br /> <br /> You only need to do as much as you need for the game. It took me less than an afternoon to be able to put together enough to do a Wild West Mage set-up and that took some poking into Werewolf books as well. (I was hoping Victorian Vampire might be a help as well... but it ended up not really giving anything substantive).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1062-ajax","name":"Ajax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1062_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2319"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T12:42:39-08:00","id":1170258,"title":"","content":"GURPS books work nicely for quick research on an era and figuring out character ideas. There was even a GURPS Mage: the Ascension for GURPS 3e with conversion guidelines.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13680-baakyocalder","name":"baakyocalder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13680_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"353"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-12-24T12:43:48-08:00","id":1170259,"title":"","content":"Oh, and GURPS bibliographies are free on the Steve Jackson Games website. You might not like all the sources, but GURPS books tend to 